# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two reasons this file matters, both learned the hard way:
#
# 1. SECRETS. The root Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file `.env`
#    (Databricks host + PAT) is copied into an image layer and persists there
#    even if a later layer deletes it. Never let credentials into the context.
#
# 2. SPEED. `.venv` alone is ~887MB; with data/, .git/ and caches the context
#    ran to hundreds of MB and the build spent minutes just transferring it.
#    Nothing here is needed at runtime: dags/ and src/ are bind-mounted for
#    live editing, data/raw is a read-only bind mount, and data/interim +
#    data/processed are named volumes (see docs/virtiofs_errno35_deadlock.md).

# --- Secrets and local config ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.databrickscfg
.claude/

# --- Virtualenvs and VCS ---
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.gitignore

# --- Generated data and run artifacts ---
data/
logs/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
.mlflow/
.airflow/

# --- Caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Not needed to serve a model ---
notebooks/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- OS noise ---
.DS_Store
